1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,933
Rocco is a clever young raccoon.

2
00:00:02,933 --> 00:00:06,166
He lives in a big, noisy town.

3
00:00:06,166 --> 00:00:09,183
Rocco has a very special talent.

4
00:00:09,183 --> 00:00:13,000
He can paint beautiful pictures with his small paws.

5
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,933
His pictures look bright and happy.

6
00:00:15,933 --> 00:00:19,716
But Rocco does not like to work hard for a long time.

7
00:00:19,716 --> 00:00:21,816
He wants fast money today.

8
00:00:21,816 --> 00:00:26,200
He wants to buy sweet cakes and soft hats without waiting.

9
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:29,950
One morning, a fat fox walks by the road.

10
00:00:29,950 --> 00:00:31,850
His name is Barnaby.

11
00:00:31,850 --> 00:00:34,850
Barnaby looks at Rocco and laughs.

12
00:00:34,850 --> 00:00:40,133
Barnaby says, "Hey, little raccoon, do you want fast money?"

13
00:00:40,133 --> 00:00:45,866
Rocco grins and says, "Yes, I want fast money right now!"

14
00:00:45,866 --> 00:00:49,433
Barnaby gives him two shiny copper coins.

15
00:00:49,433 --> 00:00:54,983
For these two coins, Rocco must wear a giant yellow banana suit.

16
00:00:54,983 --> 00:00:59,366
He must stand in front of a soup shop and wave his arms.

17
00:00:59,366 --> 00:01:02,200
The banana suit is heavy and hot.

18
00:01:02,200 --> 00:01:04,500
Many people point at Rocco.

19
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:06,183
They laugh out loud.

20
00:01:06,183 --> 00:01:11,266
Rocco feels silly, but he holds his two coins and smiles.

21
00:01:11,266 --> 00:01:15,216
The next morning, a big badger needs a worker.

22
00:01:15,216 --> 00:01:22,033
The badger says, "Carry these heavy bags of smelly trash for three coins!"

23
00:01:22,033 --> 00:01:25,783
Rocco says, "I can do that fast!"

24
00:01:25,783 --> 00:01:27,950
He picks up the big bags.

25
00:01:27,950 --> 00:01:30,466
The trash is wet and old.

26
00:01:30,466 --> 00:01:33,566
Black dirt gets on his face and fur.

27
00:01:33,566 --> 00:01:35,350
Rocco smells bad.

28
00:01:35,350 --> 00:01:41,483
His old friends, Leo the rabbit and Mia the owl, walk down the street.

29
00:01:41,483 --> 00:01:44,633
Leo and Mia stop and look at Rocco.

30
00:01:44,633 --> 00:01:48,916
Leo says, "Rocco, you are a great artist.

31
00:01:48,916 --> 00:01:52,900
Why are you carrying smelly trash for a few coins?"

32
00:01:52,900 --> 00:01:58,483
Rocco shakes his head and says, "I do not care about art, Leo!

33
00:01:58,483 --> 00:02:01,666
I have three coins in my pocket today!"

34
00:02:01,666 --> 00:02:03,866
Leo and Mia look sad.

35
00:02:03,866 --> 00:02:06,550
They turn around and walk away.

36
00:02:06,550 --> 00:02:11,150
On the third morning, a tall giraffe comes to the square.

37
00:02:11,150 --> 00:02:17,566
The giraffe says, "I need a hat, but I am too tall for normal hats!

38
00:02:17,566 --> 00:02:23,183
I will give you four coins if you stand on my head all day like a hat!"

39
00:02:23,183 --> 00:02:26,933
Rocco says, "Four coins is good money!"

40
00:02:26,933 --> 00:02:31,333
He climbs up a high tree and jumps onto the giraffe's head.

41
00:02:31,333 --> 00:02:35,450
Rocco sits there under the hot sun for six hours.

42
00:02:35,450 --> 00:02:37,866
Birds fly around his face.

43
00:02:37,866 --> 00:02:41,583
A bird tries to make a nest on Rocco's fur.

44
00:02:41,583 --> 00:02:44,783
People take funny photos with their phones.

45
00:02:44,783 --> 00:02:47,583
Rocco gets very tired and hot.

46
00:02:47,583 --> 00:02:52,033
On the fourth morning, a silly frog comes to the park.

47
00:02:52,033 --> 00:02:58,933
The frog says, "I will pay you five coins if you jump like a frog in the cold pond!"

48
00:02:58,933 --> 00:03:03,166
Rocco says, "Five coins is a big prize!"

49
00:03:03,166 --> 00:03:06,100
He jumps into the cold green water.

50
00:03:06,100 --> 00:03:08,566
He makes loud frog noises.

51
00:03:08,566 --> 00:03:09,783
Splash!

52
00:03:09,783 --> 00:03:11,000
Splash!

53
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:13,950
Many animals gather near the water.

54
00:03:13,950 --> 00:03:16,216
They throw popcorn at Rocco.

55
00:03:16,216 --> 00:03:19,000
They laugh at the silly wet raccoon.

56
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:21,083
Rocco gets very cold.

57
00:03:21,083 --> 00:03:23,716
His fur is soaked and heavy.

58
00:03:23,716 --> 00:03:30,666
He catches a cold and sneezes many times, but he collects his five small coins.

59
00:03:30,666 --> 00:03:35,433
On the fifth morning, a rich wolf walks into the market.

60
00:03:35,433 --> 00:03:40,750
The wolf says, "I need a living footstool for my big boots!

61
00:03:40,750 --> 00:03:45,383
I will pay you six coins if you lie on the cold stone floor!"

62
00:03:45,383 --> 00:03:48,650
Rocco lies down on the hard stones.

63
00:03:48,650 --> 00:03:52,950
The rich wolf puts his heavy boots on Rocco's back.

64
00:03:52,950 --> 00:03:56,816
The boots are dirty and full of small rocks.

65
00:03:56,816 --> 00:03:59,050
Rocco's back hurts a lot.

66
00:03:59,050 --> 00:04:02,133
He cannot move for two long hours.

67
00:04:02,133 --> 00:04:07,966
A big dog walks past and spills cold water on Rocco's head.

68
00:04:07,966 --> 00:04:11,983
Everyone in the market laughs at the living footstool.

69
00:04:11,983 --> 00:04:16,416
On the sixth morning, a loud rooster comes with a drum.

70
00:04:16,416 --> 00:04:24,200
The rooster says, "I will give you seven coins if you let people throw soft tomatoes at your face!"

71
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:28,566
Rocco says, "Okay, seven coins is good!"

72
00:04:28,566 --> 00:04:30,900
He stands near a wooden wall.

73
00:04:30,900 --> 00:04:33,716
Many animals buy red tomatoes.

74
00:04:33,716 --> 00:04:37,683
They throw the tomatoes at Rocco's face and chest.

75
00:04:37,683 --> 00:04:41,750
Red tomato juice goes into his eyes and ears.

76
00:04:41,750 --> 00:04:44,850
The crowds cheer and laugh loudly.

77
00:04:44,850 --> 00:04:48,200
Rocco feels small and empty inside.

78
00:04:48,200 --> 00:04:50,933
His fur is red and sticky.

79
00:04:50,933 --> 00:04:54,616
That night, Rocco walks home very slowly.

80
00:04:54,616 --> 00:04:58,066
He counts his small pile of coins on the table.

81
00:04:58,066 --> 00:05:00,833
He has twenty-seven small coins.

82
00:05:00,833 --> 00:05:02,566
But his back hurts.

83
00:05:02,566 --> 00:05:04,100
His head hurts.

84
00:05:04,100 --> 00:05:09,500
He smells like old tomatoes, pond water, and smelly trash.

85
00:05:09,500 --> 00:05:11,633
He has no friends left.

86
00:05:11,633 --> 00:05:15,283
He loses his good name for a few cheap coins.

87
00:05:15,283 --> 00:05:18,683
Rocco looks in the mirror and starts to cry.

88
00:05:18,683 --> 00:05:23,783
He says to himself, "This easy money costs too much.

89
00:05:23,783 --> 00:05:25,383
I am not a banana.

90
00:05:25,383 --> 00:05:27,100
I am not a footstool.

91
00:05:27,100 --> 00:05:28,766
I am an artist."

92
00:05:28,946 --> 00:05:32,629
The next day, Rocco makes a big decision.

93
00:05:32,629 --> 00:05:36,962
He says, "I will not do silly jobs anymore!"

94
00:05:36,962 --> 00:05:38,912
He locks his front door.

95
00:05:38,912 --> 00:05:43,529
He washes his dirty fur with warm water and soap.

96
00:05:43,529 --> 00:05:45,496
He cleans his small room.

97
00:05:45,496 --> 00:05:48,696
Then, he picks up his paint and brushes.

98
00:05:48,696 --> 00:05:54,462
He puts his small paws into bright blue, yellow, and red paint.

99
00:05:54,462 --> 00:05:57,312
He paints all day and all night.

100
00:05:57,312 --> 00:06:02,462
He paints trees, stars, rivers, and mountains.

101
00:06:02,462 --> 00:06:06,129
He paints for seven long days without stopping.

102
00:06:06,129 --> 00:06:09,362
He puts his heart into every picture.

103
00:06:09,362 --> 00:06:14,279
After one week, Rocco takes five of his best paintings.

104
00:06:14,279 --> 00:06:16,996
He walks to the central town market.

105
00:06:16,996 --> 00:06:21,129
He sets up a small wooden stall in a quiet corner.

106
00:06:21,129 --> 00:06:23,779
He places his pictures on the table.

107
00:06:23,779 --> 00:06:26,979
The sun shines on the beautiful colors.

108
00:06:26,979 --> 00:06:31,162
Rocco sits behind his table, tall and straight.

109
00:06:31,162 --> 00:06:33,312
He looks proud and clean.

110
00:06:33,312 --> 00:06:36,246
A rich bear walks past the stall.

111
00:06:36,246 --> 00:06:39,912
She wears a golden coat and black glasses.

112
00:06:39,912 --> 00:06:44,146
She owns the biggest picture gallery in the big city.

113
00:06:44,146 --> 00:06:47,429
The bear stops in front of Rocco's stall.

114
00:06:47,429 --> 00:06:51,112
She looks at one painting of a blue forest.

115
00:06:51,112 --> 00:06:52,996
Her eyes open wide.

116
00:06:52,996 --> 00:06:57,112
The bear says, "This picture is very beautiful.

117
00:06:57,112 --> 00:07:00,462
I will buy it from you for ten small coins."

118
00:07:00,462 --> 00:07:02,412
Rocco looks at the bear.

119
00:07:02,412 --> 00:07:08,396
He remembers the tall giraffe, the smelly trash, and the red tomatoes.

120
00:07:08,396 --> 00:07:10,679
He knows his work is good now.

121
00:07:10,679 --> 00:07:14,212
Rocco says, "No, thank you.

122
00:07:14,212 --> 00:07:16,229
Ten coins is too low.

123
00:07:16,229 --> 00:07:20,279
My art takes time, hard work, and love.

124
00:07:20,279 --> 00:07:24,712
The price for this painting is two hundred gold coins."

125
00:07:24,712 --> 00:07:27,079
The rich bear looks surprised.

126
00:07:27,079 --> 00:07:29,079
Then she smiles warmly.

127
00:07:29,079 --> 00:07:33,296
The bear says, "You are right, young raccoon.

128
00:07:33,296 --> 00:07:35,746
Real talent is valuable.

129
00:07:35,746 --> 00:07:39,346
I respect an artist who respects his own work.

130
00:07:39,346 --> 00:07:45,229
I will give you two hundred gold coins for this picture, and I want to buy four more!"

131
00:07:45,229 --> 00:07:49,396
She pays Rocco a big bag of heavy gold coins.

132
00:07:49,396 --> 00:07:55,112
Leo the rabbit and Mia the owl see everything from across the street.

133
00:07:55,112 --> 00:07:59,896
They see Rocco standing tall and proud with his real art.

134
00:07:59,896 --> 00:08:04,329
They walk over to his stall with big smiles on their faces.

135
00:08:04,329 --> 00:08:06,979
Mia says, "Hello, Rocco.

136
00:08:06,979 --> 00:08:09,062
Your paintings are wonderful.

137
00:08:09,062 --> 00:08:11,129
We are very happy for you."

138
00:08:11,129 --> 00:08:15,596
Rocco smiles at his old friends and says, "Thank you.

139
00:08:15,596 --> 00:08:18,679
My time is finally worth something real."

